## Lore

A Reaver Military Scout is a wilderness scout put to military use. The
skills are a woodsman''s, but the questions are a soldier''s: where a column
can hide, where an ambush should be laid, which way a fugitive ran, where
the camp goes tonight.

One or two ride with every reconnaissance, seek and destroy or covert team.
They lead patrols, blaze trails, escort, explore and run manhunts, and they
are the ones who site and conceal a base camp. They are honestly a little
worse at tracking and hunting animals than a true Wilderness Scout or a
Huntsman-Trapper, and never quite as at home among the trees.

Inside the War Camp nobody thinks of them as special: just another Reaver
who happens to know the woods. Some call them Woodsmen or Nature Boys.

## GM Notes

Hand to Hand: Expert can become Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, for one
O.C.C. Related Skill.

Starting kit beyond what the sheet lists: one weapon for each W.P. with
three extra clips apiece, a silver dagger, a wooden dagger (1D6 S.D.C.), a
hand-sized whisk broom, a flint and tinder box, a box of 100 large sealable
sample bags, plastic containers, a bedroll, belt, boots, a notepad, a
grappling hook and a handful of personal items. The armor is painted in
camouflage.

Vehicle: most Scouts have a quiet, maneuverable hovercycle assigned to them,
though many expeditions mean slow travel on foot.

Money is 1D6x100 credits plus 6D6x10 credits of tradeable goods. Salary is
600 credits a month with food, basic clothing and equipment, medical
attention and a tiny cut of the spoils of raids the Scout takes part in.

No cybernetics to start; about half pick up a bionic limb and/or a handful
of implants. Special weapons, explosives, equipment, vehicles and troops
may be issued by assignment. More weapons, special items and magic items
come through play.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'reaver-military-scout');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
